hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6106","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited him while he was not of sound mind, so he performed ablution, and some of his ablution was poured over him, and he became of sound mind. I said: He will inherit from me. Kalala, so how about inheritance? Then the verse of imposition was revealed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6107","Muhammad bin Mansour al-Makki told us, on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, who said: I heard Ibn al-Munkadir, saying: I heard Jabir, saying: I fell ill. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr came to visit me as they were walking, and they found me fainting. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and poured his ablution on me, so I woke up and said: O Messenger of God, how should I spend my money? What about my money? He did not answer me at all, until the verse of inheritance was revealed: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding the calamity.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Jurayj disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6108","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, meaning the one-eyed son of Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Al-Munkadir informed me, On the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr visited me in Bani Salamah, and they found that I had no sense, so he called for water and performed ablution. Then he sprinkled some of it on me, and I woke up, so I said to him: What should I do with my money, O Messenger of God? Then God revealed: God enjoins upon you regarding your children, for males there is an example? \The luck of two females\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6109","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Hisham told us, meaning Ibn Abi Abdullah. Al-Dastawi, who is Hisham bin Sanbar, said: Abu Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: I complained, and I have seven sisters of mine. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and blew in my face. I woke up and said: O Messenger of God, shall I not bequeath two-thirds to my sisters? Then he went out and left me, then returned to me and said: “I do not see you dead from this pain of yours, and God has sent down and made clear what is for your sisters.” So he made for them two-thirds.” Then Jabir used to say: This verse was revealed about me: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding calamity.”"
"6110","Masoud bin Juwayriyah Al-Mawsili told me, he said: Al-Mu’afa told us, on the authority of Hisham, the companion of Al-Dastawa’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I complained, and I have seven sisters of my own, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and splashed in my face. I woke up and said: “O Messenger of God.” I will leave two-thirds to my sisters. He said: Is it better? I said: Half of it. He said: Is it better? Then he left and left me. Then he came back and said: “O Jabir, I don’t.” I saw you dead from this pain of yours, and indeed, God had sent down, and made it clear to your sisters, so He gave them two-thirds.” Jabir said: So this was revealed Verse: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding calamity.”"
"6111","Yusuf bin Hammad Al-Ma’ani told us, he said: Sufyan bin Habib and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “The last verse It was revealed: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding calamity.”"
"6112","Ali ibn Hajr ibn Iyas ibn Muqatil ibn Mishmraj ibn Khalid al-Saadi al-Maruzi informed us, saying: Sa’dan, meaning ibn Yahya, told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “The last verse revealed in the Qur’an: Surah An-Nisa.”"
"6113","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Waki` told us, meaning Ibn al-Jarrah, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Qais, and his name is Abdul Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Hudhayl bin Shurahbil, who said: A man came to Abu Musa, and he is the prince, and Sufyan bin Rabi’ah Al-Bahili So he asked them about a daughter, a son’s daughter, and a sister from a father and a mother. He said: Half goes to the daughter, and what remains goes to the sister. Give Ibn Masoud. He will follow us, so the man came to Ibn Masoud and asked him, so he told him what they said. Ibn Masoud said: “I have gone astray, and I am not one of The rightly guided, but I will judge as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled: “For the daughter is half, and for the son’s daughter is a sixth, completing the two-thirds. And whatever remains is for the sister.”"
"6114","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Qais told me, he said: I heard Huzayla speaking that a man asked Abu Musa about a woman who left her daughter, her sister, and her son’s daughter. He said: For the daughter. The half, and the sister gets the half. Give Abdullah, and he will follow me. Abdullah came and mentioned that to him. He said: I found in the book, “I have Then I have gone astray, and I am not of those who are guided. I decree in it what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed: “To the daughter is half, and to the son’s daughter is a sixth. And whatever remains is for the sister.” So he came to Abu Musa and mentioned that to him, and he said: Do not ask me about anything as long as this ink is between your backs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6115","Muhammad ibn Bashar Bundar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning ghandar, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, He said: A man asked Abu Musa about a woman who left her daughter, her son’s daughter, and her sister. He said: Half to the daughter, and half to the sister. Go to Ibn Masoud, for he will follow me. So they came to Ibn Masoud and told him what Abu Musa had said. He said: “Then I have gone astray, and I am not of Those who are guided, I will decree therein according to the decree of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “For the daughter, one-half, for the son’s daughter, a sixth, and whatever remains, for the sister.” So they went to Abu Musa and told him, and he said: Do not ask me while this ink is between your backs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6116","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Hibban told us, meaning Ibn Hilal, he said: Wahib told us, meaning Ibn Khalid, he said: Ibn Tawoos told us, On the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Attach the duties to those who deserve them, so whatever remains belongs to the man most worthy of it.” \male\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6117","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Abu Dawud, meaning Omar bin Saad Al-Hafari, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn Tawus. On the authority of Tawus, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Attach money to the obligatory prayers. As long as the obligatory prayers are neglected, then the most worthy of a male man.” \. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan al-Thawri is more memorized than Wuhayb"
"6118","Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Shumail, he said: I am Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, that Omar gathered the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the matter of the grandfather, so he urged them: Whoever hears the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Did he, peace and blessings be upon him, mention anything about the grandfather? Then Maqil bin Yassar Al-Muzani stood up and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “An obligatory prayer was brought in which there was a burden, so he gave him a third, or A sixth. Omar said to him: What is the obligatory duty? He said: I do not know. Omar kicked him with his foot, then said: I did not know?"
"6119","Muhammad bin Amir Al-Masisi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told us, meaning Ibn al-Tabbaa’, he said: Hushaym told us, meaning Ibn Bashir, on the authority of Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil ibn Yasar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave a ruling regarding a grandfather who was among us for one-sixth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6120","Muawiyah bin Saleh bin Abi Ubayd Allah told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sawwar Al-Anbari, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Maqil bin Yassar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the grandfather a sixth,” so Omar said to him: Woe to you, with whom? He said: I don't know"
"6121","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abbad told us, he said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid bin Jadaan. On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: Omar asked: Whoever heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say anything about seriousness? Then a man got up and said: “I witnessed him giving him a third.” He said: With whom? He said: I don't know. He said: I don't know (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6122","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar informed us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, meaning Suleiman bin Dawud al-Tayalisi, and Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi informed us, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My son’s son has died, so what do I have of his inheritance?” So he said: One-sixth is yours. When he left, he called it and said: You have another sixth. Then when he left, he called it and said: The other sixth is food. And Muhammad said in his hadith: So when He turned around and said: “You get another sixth, and the other is your food.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6123","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq Al-Maruzi informed us. My father said: He informed us. He said: I am Abu Al-Munib Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Al-Ataki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed the grandmother a sixth, if she was not a mother.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6124","Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, saying: Ya’qub told us, meaning Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Sa’d Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, he said: Abi narrated to us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Qubaysah bin Dhu’ayb told him that the grandmother came to Abu Bakr. Al-Siddiq, she asks him her right, and he said: I don’t know anything of yours, and I will ask the people. So when the people prayed the morning prayer, he asked them, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: : I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “he gave her a sixth,” and Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone else with you? Then Muhammad bin Maslamah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, give her that, so Abu Bakr gave that to her, Ibn Shihab said. : I don’t know which of the two grandmothers she is? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6125","Mahmoud bin Khalid al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Omar told us, meaning Ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Dimashqi, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb said that the grandmother came during the reign of Abu Bakr seeking to inherit something, so Abu Bakr said: I do not find anything for you in the Book of God. Nothing, and I did not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned anything, and I will ask the people in the evening, so when he prayed the noon prayer, he stood up among the people, So he asked them. Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “give her a sixth.” He said: Did anyone with you hear that? Then Muhammad bin Maslamah called him and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving her a sixth, so Abu Bakr did that.” Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr al-Jahdhami told us, he said: I am Abd al-Ala, meaning Ibn Abd al-Ala, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, that Jeddah came to Abu Bakr, and the hadith was related to me. Muhammad bin Jablah Al-Rafiqi told me: Abdullah bin Al-Rafiqi told us. Sulaym, he said: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr al-Ruqi, told us, on the authority of Ishaq, meaning Ibn Rashid, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Dhu’ayb, that The grandmother, the mother’s mother, came to Abu Bakr and related the hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Zuhri did not hear it from Qubaisah Imran bin Bakkar Al-Barrad, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, meaning Al-Hakam bin Nafi’, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Qabisah said: She came Al-Jeddah. Harun bin Saeed bin Al-Haytham Al-Ayli told us: Khalid bin Nazar told us: I am Al-Qasim bin Mabrur. On the authority of Yunus, Ibn Shihab said: Qubaysah ibn Dhu’ayb claimed that the grandmother came to Abu Bakr, and the hadith was narrated to us Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Al-Zuhri, narrating on the authority of a man, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, that The grandmother came to Abu Bakr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6126","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Ma’n told us, meaning Ibn Isa. He said: Malik told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Uthman bin Ishaq. Ibn Kharsha, on the authority of Qubaysah Ibn Dhu’ayb, who said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr asking him for her inheritance. He said: What do you have in the Book of God? Something, and I do not know that you have anything in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so go back so that I may ask the people. So he asked the people, and Al-Mughirah b. Shu`bah: I was present with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave her a sixth. Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone else with you? Then Muhammad bin Maslamah stood up and said as Al-Mughirah had said, so Abu Bakr did it for her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6127","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, meaning Ibn Musa, he said: I am Israel, meaning Ibn Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of my father Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have more right to the believers than to themselves. So whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to the family, and whoever leaves behind wealth or loss, then I am his guardian.”"
"6128","Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, he said: Abu Usama, meaning Hammad bin Usama, on the authority of Hussein, meaning the teacher, on the authority of Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The boy did not achieve Or the father, he is his descendant, whoever he may be.” Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, he said: I heard Al-Hussein Al-Mu’allim, he said: Amr ibn Shuaib, he said: Omar said. . . sender (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6129","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammam, meaning Ibn Yahya, told us, he said: I heard Ishaq bin Abd. Allah bin Abi Talha said: Shaybah Al-Khudari told me that he witnessed Urwa speaking to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “God does not make one who has a share in Islam as one who has no share.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6130","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hunaif, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that a man threw A man with an arrow, and he killed him, and he had no heir except a maternal uncle, so Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah wrote about that to Omar, and Omar wrote: Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Allah and His Messenger are the masters of those who have no masters, and the maternal uncle is the heir of those who have no heirs.”"
"6131","Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Allah and His Messenger are the masters of those who have no masters, and the maternal uncle is the heir of those who have no heirs.” \""
6132"""
"6132","'Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad al-Harrani informed us, saying: Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from 'A'ishah, that she said: ""Allah and His Messenger are the patron (mawla) of him who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of him who has no heir."""
"6133","Harun bin Abdullah Al-Hammal told me, he said: Abu Al-Hussein Al-Ukli told me, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: I heard Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever leaves behind a debt or property, then to me, and whoever He left money, so it goes to his heir, and I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian, so I can redeem his inheritance. And he inherits his wealth.”"
"6134","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, meaning Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Badil, meaning Ibn Maysara, on the authority of Ali, meaning Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Hawzani, on the authority of Al-Miqdam Al-Kindi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am a master He who has no guardian, I inherit his wealth, and I redeem his burden."
"6135","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran Basri told us, he said: Khalid told us, and he is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Ali. On the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Hawzani, on the authority of Al-Miqdam, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever leaves behind money Then to his family, and whoever abandons both, then to God and His Messenger, and perhaps he said: Then to us. He said: I am the descendant of one who has no descendant, I inherit from him. And he is more virtuous than him, and the paternal uncle is a relative of someone who has no ancestors. He is virtuous on his behalf, and he inherits from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6136","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Qurashi told us, he said: Ibn Aidh told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the guardian of one who has no guardian. I inherit from him and pay him a ransom, and the maternal uncle is the guardian of one who has no guardian. He has no guardian, he inherits from him and pays a ransom on his behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6137","Yahya bin Musa Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When a boy receives his inheritance, he inherits, and the blessings are sent upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6138","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir Ibn Abdullah, he says in Manfus: “He inherits if his voice is heard.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, and according to al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, there is no An objectionable hadith, and Ibn Jurayj is more reliable than Al-Mughirah, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6139","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh told us, he said: I am Baqiyya, meaning Ibn al-Walid, he said: Abu Salamah al-Homsi told me, on the authority of Omar bin Ru’bah, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Abdullah Al-Nasri, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ A woman gets three inheritances: her freed man, her foundling, and the child over whom she cursed.”"
"6140","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Harb, he said: Omar bin Ruba told us, he said: I entered with Abu Salamah al-Humsi over him, He told us on the authority of Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, on the authority of Wathilah ibn al-Asqa’, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “A woman should attain Three inheritances: her freed man, her foundling, and her child whom she cursed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6141","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, he said: Ibn Aidh told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, he said: Thawr bin told me Yazid, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a man from the Ansar from the Banu Zurayq slandered his wife, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he repeated that four times to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then God revealed the cursed verse, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Where is the questioner? Indeed, a great matter has come down from God, so the man refused to say nothing.” He cursed her, but she refused to avoid the torment for herself, so she cursed us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Either she brings him yellow Akhinas pickled bones, it is for the cursed, or she brought it as black as a camel, then it is for someone else, so she brought it black Like a camel with leaves. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and placed him on his mother’s side, and said: If the oaths that passed away had not been there, it would have been mine. \Therein is such-and-such.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6142","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: It was Omar, he says: The blood money is obligatory for the sane woman, and the woman does not inherit anything from her husband’s blood money. Al-Dahhak bin Sufyan said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote To him: “That the wife of Ashim Al-Dababi inherited from her husband’s blood money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6143","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, saying: Omar bin Al-Khattab is the blood money for a sane woman, and the woman does not inherit anything from her husband’s blood money.” Al-Dahhak Al-Kilabi even testified that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He wrote to him: “To make the wife of Ashim Al-Dababi inherit from her husband’s blood money,” so Omar returned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6144","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Yahya bin Sa’id, meaning Al-Ansari, told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: A group of people asked in Mina: Who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say a word about it? Al-Dahhak bin Sufyan Al-Kilabi, who used it to give charity to the Banu Kilab, said: I have knowledge of him, so Omar said: He said a word that meant: Wait for me until I come out, so he entered a room, stayed there for an hour, then came out and told the people that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He wrote to him: “To make a woman inherit more than her husband’s blood money.” So he returned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6145","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa bin Maadan told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, he said: Yahya told us. Ibn Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Zuhri Ibn Shihab, that Omar asked him for blood money at Mina regarding a woman’s inheritance from her husband’s aql, so Al-Dahhak said Ibn Sufyan Al-Kallabi: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to me: “To bequeath to the wife of Ashim al-Dhababi some of her husband’s blood money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6146","Ali bin Hajr bin Iyas Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, and Yahya bin Saeed, and he mentioned The last of the three of them, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The murderer has no one to \Inheritance is something\"""""
"6147","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The killer has nothing to do with it.”"
"6148","On the authority of Qutayba, Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The murderer does not inherit.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ishaq’s hadith is abandoned. I included it in Mashaykh al-Layth so that he would not be left out of the middle."
"6149","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: I am Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “It was abrogated from this Surah, meaning two verses: the verse about necklaces, and its saying: If they come to you, judge. between them or turn away from them, return them to their rulers, until it was revealed: And to judge between them according to what God has revealed. He said: Then the Messenger of God was commanded May God bless him and grant him peace to judge between them according to what God has revealed"
"6150","Muhammad bin Bashar Bundar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Jafar, in Ghandar, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6151","Ahmad ibn Harb informed us, saying: Qasim, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Jarmi, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, meaning Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Issa, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel, nor does \the infidel Muslim\"""""
"6152","Muhammad bin Salamah Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry told us, he said: I am Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Omar bin Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6153","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim Al-Khalal Al-Maruzi told us, he said: I am Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: I am Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit \unbeliever\"""""
"6154","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahwi told us, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Othman bin Affan, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Like him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct view from the hadith of Malik is: Omar bin Uthman, and we do not know that any of al-Zuhri’s companions followed him on that. It was said to him, so he stood firm and said: This is his home. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6155","Qutayba bin Saeed bin Jamil bin Tarif al-Balkhi and Abu Marru al-Harith bin Miskin told us, after reading it, and I was hearing about... Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel, nor does an infidel inherit from a Muslim.”"
"6156","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Othman. On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The infidel does not inherit from the Muslim, and the Muslim does not inherit from the infidel.”"
"6157","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ali Bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An infidel does not inherit from a Muslim. The Muslim does not inherit from the infidel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6158","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, On the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The infidel does not inherit from the Muslim, nor does the Muslim \unbeliever\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6159","Wahb bin Bayan Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, On the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Usama ibn Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit an infidel, nor does he inherit \the infidel Muslim\"""""
"6160","Masoud bin Juwayriyah Al-Mawsili told me, he said: Hushaym told us, meaning Ibn Bashir, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, and Aban bin Othman, and so he said: On the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People of two different sects do not inherit inheritance.”"
"6161","Ali bin Hajr bin Iyas Al-Maruzi told us, saying: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, On the authority of Osama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People of two religions do not inherit one another.”"
"6162","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr Al-Jahdhami told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amir Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People of two religions do not inherit inheritance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6163","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ata’, and others, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People of two different religions do not inherit inheritance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6164","Masoud bin Juwayriyah al-Mawsili told me, he said: Thana al-Mu’afa, meaning Ibn Imran al-Mawsili, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, my father, Al-Hakam Rafi’, that he converted to Islam, and his wife refused to accept Islam, so she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my daughter. He said: This is weaned, or almost weaned. Abu al-Hakam said: O Messenger of God, my daughter. Then the Prophet said to him: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Sit near him, and he said to her: Sit near him, and the boy sat between them, then he said: Call him, so the girl turned. To her mother, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, guide her.” So she turned to her father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6165","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid al-Ansari. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he converted to Islam, but his wife refused to embrace Islam, so a young son of theirs who had not reached puberty came, and the Prophet sat down. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The father is here, and the mother is here. Then he gave him a choice and said: “O God, guide him,” so he went to his father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6166","Mujahid bin Musa Al-Baghdadi told us, saying: Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Aliya, on the authority of Uthman Al-Batti, on the authority of Abdul-Hamid bin Salamah. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that his parents disputed about him before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them was a Muslim, and the other was an infidel, so he decided to To the infidel, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, guide him.” So he turned to the Muslim and decided for him. Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, meaning Ibn Hammad al-Narsi, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, that a man converted to Islam, but his wife did not convert to Islam. . . sender (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6167","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadfi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr al-Yafi’i informed me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Christian Muslim does not inherit, unless his servant “or his female slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6168","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya informed me. He said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Harun. He said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub. On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If the decree bequeaths a punishment, or an inheritance, and he inherits according to what He was freed from it, and the punishment was imposed on him on account of what he freed from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6169","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani informed us, he said: Ours is Khaled, meaning Ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Asbahani, that he heard Mujahid, narrating on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that she mentioned that a servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, died, so they mentioned his inheritance to him, and he said: “Is there anyone from his land here? They said: Yes, so he said: So give him to him.” Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, meaning the one-eyed son of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Asbahani, on the authority of Mujahid bin Wardan, a man from the people of Medina, who praised him well, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. . . Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6170","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa and Muhammad ibn Bashar Bundar informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi. He said: Sufyan told us, meaning Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Isbahani, on the authority of Mujahid bin Wardan, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that Mawla The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell down from the stalk of a palm tree and died. Then his inheritance was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Does he have any relatives or relatives?” Lineage? They said: No. He said: Look at some of his family, and Ibn Bashar said: The family of his people, so give it to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6171","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna Abu Musa informed us, on the authority of Abu Ahmad, whose name is Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zuhri, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Gabriel bin Ahmar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a man from Khuza’ah died, leaving no heir, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: “They looked for a group for him, but they did not find any, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give him the largest Khuza’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6172","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal Al-Raqqi told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Abbad told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of God, I have the inheritance of a man from Azd, and I have not Shall I find a young man to pay him to? He said: Go, and look for a young man, or he said: A year, so he set off, then he came to him at dawn of the second year, and said: O Messenger of God, I did not find a Azadi. He said: Go, and give him to the first Khuza’i he met. When he turned away, he said: The man is upon me, so he returned. So he said: Go, and push him to the largest Khuza’ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6173","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samra al-Kufi informed us, Ahmad ibn Harb al-Mawsili informed us, saying: The warrior told us, and his name is Abdul Rahman. Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Jibril Ibn Ahmar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: He said: “I have the inheritance of a man from Azd, and I cannot find a Azdi to pay it to.” He said: “Go and look for a Azdi,” and he came to him after the year. He said to him: I did not find a man to whom I could pay him. He said: So go and see the best Khuza’ah. Muhammad bin Ismail said: The elder of Khuza’ah. So give it to him.” Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Gabriel bin Ahmar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, he said: A man came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have in my hand the inheritance of a man from Azd. . . The chain of the hadith is mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6174","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi informed us, saying: Husayn bin Ali Al-Jafi told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Hamza’s daughter, he said: “A servant of mine died, and left his daughter, so he divided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided his wealth between me and his daughter, so he gave me half, and half to her.” Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, said: She is the maternal sister of his son Shaddad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6175","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Had, that the daughter of Hamza bin Abdul-Muttalib “emancipated a mamluk of hers, and he died and left His daughter and his mistress, so his daughter inherited half, and Hamzah’s daughter inherited half.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it."
"6176","Muhammad ibn Bashar Bundar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she wanted to buy Bureerah for emancipation, but her masters wanted to stipulate her loyalty, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “ Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6177","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning the revolutionary, narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loyalty belongs to the one who is given the gift and the one who is bestowed with blessings.”"
"6178","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I bought Bareerah Her family stipulated her loyalty, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Emancipate her, for loyalty belongs to the one who gave the paper.” She said: So I freed her (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6179","Nasr bin Ali al-Jahdhami told us, he said: I am Abd al-Ala, meaning the sublime son of Abd al-Ala. They said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa. On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loyalty is only to the one who is freed.”"
"6180","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Homsi informed us, saying: Uthman, meaning Ibn Sa`id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar, on the authority of Shuaib, al-Zuhri said: Urwah said, Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Loyalty belongs to the one who is freed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6181","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Ja`far, in Ghandar, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, he said: I heard Al-Qasim speaking, on the authority of Aisha, that she wanted to buy Bareerah for emancipation, and that they stipulated her loyalty. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to whom.” emancipated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6182","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, that she bought Bureerah from some of the Ansar, and they stipulated loyalty, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “Loyalty is to him who is bestowed with blessings.”"
"6183","Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahhawi, Muhammad ibn Ismail, and Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, saying: Ja`far ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Bareerah came to ask me for help in writing to her, so I said to her: If your master wishes, I paid them your price for one sacrifice, and I freed you. So Bareerah mentioned this to her masters, and they said: No, unless you stipulate that loyalty For us, she said: So I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said, “Buy it, for loyalty belongs to the one who is freed.” The pronunciation is for Ahmad. Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra Barira came to seek Aisha’s help. . . sender (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6184","Qutayba bin Saeed bin Jamil bin Tarif Al-Balkhi told us, saying: Sufyan told us, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Awsaja speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “A man died during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he left no relatives, except a slave. He freed him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him his inheritance.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Awsaja is not well-known, and we do not know that anyone narrated on his authority other than Amr ibn Dinar, and we did not find this. Hadith except when it is difficult (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6185","Abu Dawud, whose name is Suleiman bin Saif al-Harrani, told us, he said: Abu Asim, whose name is al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid, told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, that a man died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They looked for an heir for him, but they did not find an heir, so he gave his inheritance to the one who He freed him from his descendants.” I said: Who spoke to you? He said: Awsaja, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6186","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna Abu Musa Al-Anazi told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Wahb, on the authority of Tamim, meaning the one with the knowledgeable one, said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man from among the polytheists who greeted a man from among the polytheists. Muslims, he said: “He is closest to people in terms of his life and death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6187","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Aqeel Al-Basri told us, he said: My grandfather told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: Abdul told me Al-Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mawhib, I heard him, narrating Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Tamim Al-Dari said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: Did you see a man from the people of infidels greeting him at the hands of a man from the people of Islam, how is the judiciary done for him? He said: “He is the most deserving of people in his life and death.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6188","Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man from among the polytheists who would greet the man’s hands. Among the Muslims, he said: “He is the closest of people to it, in his life and in his death.”"
"6189","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawareb al-Qurashi informed us of Basri, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6190","Ali bin Hajr bin Iyas Al-Maruzi told us, on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of loyalty and the gift of it.”"
"6191","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq Al-Kufi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, and Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling loyalty and giving it away.”"
"6192","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told us, he said: Abu Usama, whose name is Hammad bin Usama, told us: Idris bin Yazid told me, he said Talha bin Musrif narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: And to those whose oaths are tied, give them their share. He said: “When the immigrants came to Medina, the Ansar were given inheritance, without any ties of kinship, to the brothers whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood among them. When it was revealed: And for each of us We have appointed a follower from among what the parents and the relatives have left behind, he said: It was abrogated: And to whom your oaths are bound, go to them. Their share of victory, advice, and support, and will be made for him, and the inheritance has gone."
"6193","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi informed us, saying: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no swearing in Islam, and whatever An oath that existed during pre-Islamic times, Islam only made it more severe.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6194","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, on the authority of Asad bin Musa, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Tell me Rashid bin Saad, that he heard Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib Al-Kindi, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever abandons a debt, or Lost, then it goes to me, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to his heirs, and I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian, I am wiser to him, and I inherit his wealth, and the uncle is my guardian. “Whoever has no guardian, his bondage will be released and he will inherit his wealth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6195","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar told me. He said: Baqiyya told us, meaning Ibn al-Walid. He said: Abu Salamah Sulayman told me. Ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Omar Ibn Ru’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, on the authority of Wathilah Ibn al-Asqa’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A woman gets three inheritances: her freed man, her foundling, and her child for whom she curses.”"
"6196","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, he said: “The Messenger of God did not leave God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not a dinar, nor a dirham, nor a male slave, nor a female slave, except for his grey-haired mule that he was riding, his weapons, and land. He made it for the sake of God.” Qutaibah said again: “Charity.”"
"6197","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, he said: I heard Amr Ibn Al-Harith said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave anything behind except his white mule, his weapons, and land that he left as charity.”"
"6198","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Amr bin Al-Harith says: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and he left behind nothing but his white mule, his weapons, and some land that he left as charity.”"
"6199","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: “I afflicted some land in the land of Khaybar, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I afflicted I have not acquired anything dear to me, nor do I own any of it. He said: “If you wish, you can give it in charity, then give it in charity, provided that it is sold and not given as a gift. Concerning the poor, relatives, slaves, guests, and the wayfarer, there is no blame on the one who is her guardian to eat in a reasonable manner, without spending money. And he feeds.” Harun bin Abdullah Al-Bazzar informed me, saying: Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6200","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: Omar acquired land in Khaybar, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I acquired land that I had never acquired more money than, so how? Do you order it? He said: “If you wish, you can keep its originals and give them in charity, so Omar gave them in charity on the condition that its originals will not be sold, given away, or inherited, to the poor. And relatives, and slaves, and for the sake of God, and guests, and the wayfarer, there is no sin on the one who is in charge of them if he eats from it in a reasonable manner, and feeds \Truthful"
"6201","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun. Humayd ibn Masada told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar hit the ground In Khaybar, he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and asked him to appoint him there, and he said: I have acquired land in Khaybar, and I have never acquired any wealth that I have ever lost. From it, what do you command regarding it? He said: “If you wish, you can withhold its principal and give it in charity, so give it in charity, provided that its principal cannot be sold, given away, or inherited, so give it in charity.” It is used for the poor, or relatives, and for freeing slaves, and in the path of God, and the wayfarer, and the guest. There is no blame, then it was cut off. Ali bin Muawiyah, Or feed an ungrateful friend.” The word is for Ishmael (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6202","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Azhar al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar hit the ground In Khaybar, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to consult him about that, and he said: “If you wish, you can withhold its originals and give it in charity.” So he withheld Its origin is that it should not be sold, given away, or bequeathed, so give it in charity to the poor, relatives, slaves, the needy, and the wayfarer. As for the guest, there is no sin on the one who is its guardian if he eats from it in a reasonable manner, or feeds his friend without being greedy for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6203","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ al-Basri told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas He said: When this verse was revealed: You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, Abu Talha said: I see our Lord asking us of our wealth. So I bear witness to you, O Messenger of God, that I have made my land for God. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Put it among your relatives, in Hassan.” Ibn Thabit and Ubayy Ibn Ka’b.”"
"6204","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makki told us, he said: Sufyan, he is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The hundred shares that I have in Khaybar, I have never had any more money than them. I wanted to give it in charity. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Withhold its root, and cause its fruit to spill.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6205","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khalanji told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He came Omar went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have acquired wealth, the like of which I have never acquired. I had a hundred heads. So I bought one hundred shares with it in Khaybar from its people, and I wanted to draw closer to God Almighty with it. He said: “Then withhold its original. \And the path of fruit\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6206","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa ibn Bahloul informed us, saying: Baqiyya informed us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Salim al-Makki, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a piece of land for me. He said: “Withhold its roots, and \its fruit\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6207","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamar bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard my father, speaking on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Amr bin Javan, a man from Banu Tamim, and that is because I said to him: Did you see the isolation of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, what happened? He said: I heard Al-Ahnaf saying: I am a Hajj, while we were in our homes putting our bags, when someone came and said: The people have gathered in the mosque. So I set off and saw the people gathered, and a group of people sitting between their backs. Then, it was Ali bin Abi Talib, al-Zubayr, and Talha. And Saad bin Abi Waqqas. When I stood up to them, it was said: This is Uthman bin Affan. I have come to Medina. He said: Then he came wearing a yellow robe. I said to my friend: As you are, so that I can see what he brought with him. Uthman said: Did Ali bin Abi Talib insult us? Is Zubair insulting us? Is there Talha here? Is this Saad bin Abi Waqqas here? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys “The nest of the son of so-and-so, may God forgive him.” So I bought it, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I have bought the house of the son of so-and-so,” he said. So put it in our mosque, and its reward is yours? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He buys the well of Rumah, may God forgive him.” So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have bought the well of Rumah. He said: So make it Is it watering for the Muslims, and its reward is yours? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He prepares the army of hardship, may God forgive him.” So I prepared them, so that they would not lose either head or foot? They said: Yes, he said: O God, bear witness, O God, bear witness, O God, bear witness."
"6208","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdullah bin Idris informed us, he said: I heard Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, speaking about Omar Bin Jawan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qays, who said: We went out as pilgrims, so we came to Medina, and we wanted to perform Hajj, so while we were in our homes, we placed We were on our way, when someone came to us and said: The people have gathered in the mosque, and they were terrified, so we set off, and behold, the people were gathered in a group in the middle of The mosque, and behold, Ali, Al-Zubayr, Talha, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas were there, when Othman bin Affan came, wearing a blanket. Yellow, he covered his head with it and said: Is Ali here? Is there Talha here? Is Zubair insulting us? Is this Saad here? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “He bought the shelter of the son of so-and-so, may God forgive him.” So I bought it for twenty thousand, or for twenty-five thousand, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I told him, and he said: Put it in our mosque, and its reward is yours? They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “He buys the well of Rumah, may God forgive him.” So I bought it for such-and-such, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “You have bought it.” With such and such, he said: Make it water for the Muslims, and its reward is yours? They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked into the faces of The people, and he said: “Whoever equips these people, may God forgive him,” meaning the army of hardship. So you equipped them so that they did not lose their head or their shoulders? They said: Oh God, yes. He said: Oh God, bear witness. Oh God, bear witness."
"6209","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Sa`id bin Amir told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Sa`id al-Jariri, on the authority of Thumama bin Al-Qushayri was sad and said: I saw the house when Othman supervised them and said: I adjure you by God and Islam. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace. He came to Medina, and there was no available water in it other than the well of Rumah, and he said: “Whoever buys the well of Rumah and puts in it Is his bucket with the buckets of the Muslims, better for him than it in Paradise? So I bought it with my own money, and put in it my bucket with the buckets of the Muslims? Today, you prevent me from drinking from it, until I drink sea water! ! They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him, and Islam. Do you know that I prepared the army of hardship with my own money? They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God and Islam. Do you know that the mosque is crowded with its people? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Who would buy the plot of so-and-so’s family and increase it in the mosque, with something better for him than it in Paradise?” So I bought it with my own money. So I increased it in the mosque, and you prevent me from praying two rak’ahs there! ! They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God and Islam. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with Thubair? Mecca, and with him were Abu Bakr, Omar, and me. Then the mountain moved, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ran over it with his foot, and said: Be still, Thabeer. Indeed, upon you is a prophet, a truthful, and two witnesses. They said: Oh God, yes. He said: God is great. They bear witness for me and the Lord of the Kaaba. It means: I am a martyr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6210","Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid Al-Homsi told me, he said: Khattab, Ibn Uthman Al-Homsi, told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, He said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that Uthman supervised them when they besieged him, and he said: “I implore you By God, a man heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say one day when the mountain shook, so he kicked it with his foot and said: “Be still, for it “None is upon you except a prophet, or a truthful, or a martyr.” And I was with him. He said: So men called out to him, then he said: I seek for God’s sake a man who has borne witness. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the Pledge of Ridwan, said: “This is the hand of God, and this is the hand of Othman,” so men chanted for him, then He said: I seek the help of God of a man who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on the Day of the Army of Hardship: “Who will spend an acceptable expenditure? So I prepared half the army with my own money.” So he called out men for him, then he said: “I call upon God for a man who has heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He says: “Who can add a house in Paradise to this mosque? “So I bought it with my own money, and some men cried out for it, then he said: I seek by God a man who witnessed a Roman being sold, so I bought it with my own money. So I made it permissible for a wayfarer, and men looked for him.” Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, said: When Uthman was confined to his house, and people gathered around his house, he stood up and supervised them. . . The chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6211","Ahmad bin Harb Al-Mawsili told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara, and he is Ibn Al-Qaqa’ Kufi, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah Kufi, who is Ibn Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, Which charity has the greatest reward? He said: To give charity when you are healthy and stingy, fear poverty, and hope to survive, and do not delay, even when you have reached it. “Halloum,” “I said so-and-so to so-and-so, and it was to so-and-so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6212","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Which of you is more beloved to him than his heir’s money than his own?” They said: O Messenger of God, there is not one of us except His wealth is more beloved to him than the wealth of his heir, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Know that it is not from you from anyone, except the wealth of his heir.” “More beloved to him than his wealth is what you give back, and the wealth of your heir what you give back.”"
"6213","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa`id, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You were distracted by multiplication {1} until you visited graves {2}. He said: The son of Adam says: Mali, “Your wealth is only what you ate and did not use up, or what you put on and did not use it, or what you gave in charity and did not do well.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6214","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, Abu Habiba heard Al-Ta'i, he said: A man bequeathed dinars for the sake of God, so Abu Al-Darda' was asked, and he narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: \For example He who frees"
"6215","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “A Muslim person who has something to be bequested to has no right to stay for two nights unless he has his will written.”"
"6216","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “It is not the right of a Muslim person who has something to be bequeathed to him to stay for two nights unless his will is written with him.” Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym al-Marwazi told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’ On the authority of Ibn Umar. . . His saying (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6217","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He is safe. He told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not the right of a person to spend three nights without having his will.” Abdullah bin Omar said: Not a night has passed since I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that, unless I have my will. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6218","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Wazir ibn Sulayman al-Masry informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus and Amr ibn Al-Harith is the son of Ya’qub, an Egyptian. Malik narrated from him, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the right of a Muslim man who has something to be bequeathed to him to stay for three nights unless his will is written with him?”"
"6219","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari Al-Basri told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, he said: Talha told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recommend? He said: No, I said: How was the will prescribed for Muslims? He said: “He recommended the Book of God.”"
"6220","Hanad bin Al-Sari told me, Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ told me, and Ahmad bin Harb told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, And Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Favorable narration, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave behind a dinar, a dirham, a sheep, or a camel, nor did he leave anything bequeathed.” Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ said in his hadith: Al-A’mash told us (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6221","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Mus’ab told us, and he is Ibn al-Miqdam Kufi, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave behind a dirham, nor a dinar, nor a sheep, nor a camel. And he did not command.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6222","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin al-Hudhayl al-Kufi told us, and Ahmad bin Yusuf al-Naysaburi told us, saying: Asim bin Yusuf told us, he said: Hassan told us Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave behind a dirham. Nor a dinar, nor a sheep, nor a camel, nor a will.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6223","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Azhar told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: They say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a will for Ali! He called for a basin to urinate in, and his soul became effeminate.” He prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not feel, to whom should he recommend?"
"6224","Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Nasa’i told me, and its origin is Maruzi, he said: ‘Arim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and no one was with him but me,” she said: He called for the basin.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The correct hadith is the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, Mufaddal, Dawud, and the hadith of Ibn Ayyash. We do not know that anyone followed him on his statement: On the authority of Abraham, on the authority of the lions"
"6225","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed told me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: I fell ill. I recovered from it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me to visit me, and I said: “O Messenger of God, I have a lot of wealth, and no one will inherit me except my daughter.” Should I give two-thirds of my money in charity? He said: No, I said: The half? He said: No, I said: The third? He said: A third is a lot, if you give up “If your heirs are rich, it is better for them than for you to leave them poor, begging others.”"
"6226","Amr bin Mansour and Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, and the wording is for Ahmad, they said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me to visit me, while I was in Mecca. I said: “Oh Messenger of God, should I bequeath all of my wealth? He said: No. I said: The half? He said: No. I said: The third? He said: A third? And a third is a lot? “It is better for your heirs to be rich, than to leave them poor, begging people to begrudge themselves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6227","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, On the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit him while he was in Mecca, and he hated to die in the land from which he emigrated. He said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on Saad bin Afra. May God have mercy on Saad bin Afra, and he only had one daughter. He said: O Messenger of God, should I bequeath all of my wealth? He said: No. He said: Half? He said: No. I said: A third? He said: A third? And a third is a lot. If you leave it to your heirs? It is better for them to be rich than to leave them poor, begging people for what they have.” Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: Some of the family of Saad, he said: Saad fell ill, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and said: O Messenger of God, should I make a bequest of all my wealth? He said: “No... and the chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6228","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari Al-Basri told us, he said: Abdul-Kabir bin Abdul Majeed told us, he said: Bukayr told us Ibn Mismar said: I heard Amer ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, that he complained in Mecca, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him, and when Saad saw him and cried, and said: “O Messenger of God, I will die in the land from which you emigrated.” He said: No, God willing, and he said: O Messenger of God, I will give my will With all of my money for the sake of God? He said: No. He said: And he mentioned a word that means it. He said: So with two-thirds of it? He said: No. He said: So with half of it? He said: No. He said: A third of it? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A third, and a third is great. If you leave your children rich, “It is better than to leave them destitute, begging people.”"
"6229","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sa’d ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited me during my illness, and he said: “Did you make a will?” I said: Yes, he said: How much? I said: With all my money for the sake of God. He said: What have you left for your children? I said: They are wealthy. He said: I bequeath a tithe. He continued saying and I say, until he said: I bequeath. One-third, and one-third is a lot, or a large amount.”"
"6230","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He visited him during his illness. He said: “O Messenger of God, should I bequeath all of my wealth?” He said: No. He said: The half? He said: No. He said: The third? He said: a third, and a third is a lot, or a large one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6231","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham told us about Baghdadi, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabi’ah Kufi told us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Saad to visit him, and Saad said to him: “O Messenger of God, will I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth?” He said: No. He said: Should I bequeath half? He said: No. He said: Should I bequeath a third? He said: Yes, a third. Is a third a lot, or a large amount? It is better to leave your heirs rich than to leave them poor and belittle themselves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6232","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “If he had overlooked people to a quarter, because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A third, and a third is a lot, or a large amount.”"
"6233","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, On the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father Saad bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him while he was sick, and said: I have no son except One daughter, so I will bequeath all my wealth? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. He said: So should I bequeath half of it? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. He said: So should I bequeath a third of it? He said: “One-third, and one-third is a big deal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6234","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, he said: Jabir bin told me Abdullah said, “His father was martyred on the day of Uhud, and he left behind six daughters, and left a debt he owed. When the date-palm shearer came, I came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: You have learned that my father was martyred on the day of Uhud, and left behind a large debt, and I would love for the debtors to see you. He said: “ Go, and he scattered every date in one direction, so I did, then I called him, and when they looked at him, it was as if they had been deceived by me at that hour, and when he saw what They were making. He went around a threshing floor around the largest of them three times, then he sat on it, then he said: Call your companions. He continued to measure to them, until he had finished. “God is my father’s trust, and I am satisfied that God fulfills my father’s trust, not a single date is missing.”"
"6235","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq told us, who is the son of Yusuf al-Azraq al-Wasiti, he said: Zakariya told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, said that his father died owing a debt, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of God, my father has died.” He owed a debt, and he only left behind what his palm trees produced, and his palm trees did not produce the debt he owed for less than two years, so go with me. O Messenger of God, so that the creditors do not slander me. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to one of the farms, walked around it and said goodbye. He sat on it, and called the creditors, and paid them back, and left what they had received.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6236","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Abdullah bin Amr bin died. It is forbidden. He said: He left a debt, so I sought intercession with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his creditors to put aside some of his debt. So he asked them, They refused, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Go and sort your dates into different types, the ajwa separately, and the dates of Zayd separately. And its types, then he sent to me. He said: So I did, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and sat in the upper part, or in the middle of it, then he said “Eat for the people.” He said: “So I ate for them until I repaid them, then my dates remained as if nothing had been missing from them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6237","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad al-Tartusi Harami told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said: A Jew had power over Abu Tamr, and he was killed on the day of Uhud, leaving two gardens, and the Jew absorbed what was in it. The two gardens, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Can you take part of the year and delay part of it?” The Jew refused, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: O Jabir, when the grandfather comes, call me to announce it, and I announce to him. Then he and Abu Bakr came, and he began to speak hard and be measured by Under the palm trees, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for blessing, until he paid us all his rights from the smaller of the two gardens, according to Ammar’s calculations. Then I brought them fresh dates and water, and they ate and drank. Then he said: This is from the bliss that you are asked about.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6238","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He died. My father owed a debt, so I proposed to his creditors that they should take the fruit for what he owed, but they refused, and they did not see that there was any repayment in it, so I came to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so I mentioned that to him. He said: “If you renew it, then put it in the cemetery, then let me know.” So when you renewed it, then put it in the Al-Murbad, I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar came with him. He sat on him and invoked blessings, then he said: Pray. Your debtors, and repay them. He said: I never left anyone who owed my father a debt without paying it off, and he left me thirteen wasqs in surplus, so I mentioned that to him. He laughed and said: Go to Abu Bakr and Omar and tell them that. So I went to Abu Bakr and Omar and told them, and they said: We know. “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did what he did, it will be that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6239","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Amr bin Kharijah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech and said: “Indeed, God has given everyone his right, so no \a will to an heir\"""""
"6240","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, That Ibn Ghanam mentioned, that Ibn Kharijah mentioned, that he witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressing the people on his camel, and that it To be licked with its jug, and its saliva was flowing. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his sermon: “Indeed, God has allotted to every human being His share of the inheritance, so it is not permissible for an heir to make a will.”"
"6241","Utba bin Abdullah Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Amr bin Kharijah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has given everyone his due right, so there is no will for an heir.”"
"6242","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: When it was revealed: And warn your closest relatives, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called the Quraysh, and they gathered, and he spoke in general and in particular, and said: “O my son Ka'b bin Luayy, O Banu Murrah bin Ka'b, O Banu Abd Shams, O Banu Abd Manaf, O Banu Hashim, and O Banu Abd Al-Muttalib, save yourselves from the Fire, O Fatima, save yourself from the Fire. I do not possess anything for you from God, except that you have mercy. “I will make her wet with my own wetness.”"
"6243","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Muawiyah, who is the son of Ishaq, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O sons of Abd Manaf, buy yourselves from your Lord, for I do not own anything for you.” Something from God. O children of Abdul Muttalib, buy from your Lord. Indeed, I do not possess anything for you from God, but there is a bond between me and you. I am mindful of it. \By her wetness\"""""
"6244","Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa`id bin al-Musayyab informed me, And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when it was revealed to him: “And warn Your closest clan. He said: O people of Quraysh, buy yourselves from God. I am of no use to you before God. O sons of Abdul Muttalib, I am of no use to you. I am of no use to you from God, O Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib. I am of no use to you from God, O Safiyya, aunt of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “I am of no use to you before God. O Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, ask me whatever you wish. I am of no use to you before God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6245","Muhammad bin Khalid told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab told me, And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when it was revealed to him: “And warn Your closest clan, and he said: O people of Quraysh, buy yourselves from God. I am of no use to you from God. O Banu Abd Manaf, I am of no use to you. I am of no use to you from God, O Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, I am of no use to you before God, O Safiyya, the aunt of the Messenger of God, I am of no use to you. God is willing, O Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, ask me whatever you want, I am of no use to you before God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6246","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When This verse was revealed: “And warn your closest relatives. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, O Safiyya, daughter of Abdul-Muttalib, O sons of Abdul-Muttalib, I am of no use to you before God, ask me of my wealth whatever you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6247","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that A man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “My mother has lost herself, and if she spoke, she would give in charity. Should I give charity on her behalf?” He said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Yes, so he gave alms on her behalf. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6248","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading about it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Amr bin Shurahbil bin Saad Ibn Ubadah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: “Saad Ibn Ubadah went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his battles, and his mother was present.” She died in Medina, and it was said to her: I will make a will. She said: What will I bequeath to? The money is Sa’d’s property. She died before Sa’d arrived. When Sa’d arrived, This was mentioned to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, will it benefit her if I give alms on her behalf? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. Saad said: Such-and-such wall is a charity on her behalf, for a wall he named. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6249","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Al-Alaa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If a person dies, his deeds cease, except for three: ongoing charity, beneficial knowledge, or a righteous child.” pray for him\""
6250"""
"6250","'Ali ibn Hujr informed us, saying: Isma'il informed us, saying: Al-'Ala' narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""My father died and left wealth, and did not make a bequest; will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf?"" He said: ""Yes."""
"6251","Musa bin Saeed Al-Tartusi told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Al-Sharid bin Suwayd Al-Thaqafi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My mother commanded that I emancipate She has a slave, and I have a Nubian slave girl. Would it be sufficient for me if I freed her on her behalf? He said: Bring her to me. So I brought her to him, and he said to her? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Who is your Lord? She said: God. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of God. He said: So free her, for she is the one. “faithful” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6252","Al-Hussein bin Issa informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Saad asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “My mother died without leaving a will. Should I give alms on her behalf?” He said: “Yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6253","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ruh bin Ubadah told us, he said: Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, he said: Amr told us Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man said: “O Messenger of God, his mother has died. Will it benefit her if I give in charity?” On her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: I have a sheep, and I bear witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf."
"6254","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Sulayman bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Saad ibn Ubadah, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother died, and upon her A vow, will it suffice for her if I free her from her? He said: “Emancipate your mother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6255","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqi Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani told me, on the authority of Isa, who is Ibn Yunus, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Saad Ibn Ubadah, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fatwa regarding a vow he had made to his mother. She died before she could fulfill it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fulfill it on her behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6256","Muhammad bin Sadaqa told me, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he told him on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abd By God, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Saad bin Ubadah, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fatwa regarding a vow he had made to his mother, and she died before To fulfill it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fulfill it on her behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6257","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Beiruti told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Ibn Shihab told me Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Saad asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fatwa about “a vow he had made.” His mother died before she could fulfill it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fulfill it on her behalf.”"
"6258","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Saad bin Ubadah asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fatwa about a vow he had made to his mother, and she died before she could fulfill it. He said: Fulfill it. \about her\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"6259","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Saad, that he said: “My mother died and she had a vow, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered me to fulfill it on her behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6260","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Saad bin Ubadah Al-Ansari consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a vow he had made to his mother, and she died before she could fulfill it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Make it up for her.”"
"6261","Harun bin Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Bakr bin Wael, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Saad bin Ubadah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My mother died and she owed a vow that she did not fulfill? He said: Make it up for her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6262","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Ubadah said: I said: O Messenger of God, my mother has died, should I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes, I said: Which charity is better? He said: “Irrigating water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6263","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ubadah, he said: I said: “O Messenger of God, which charity is better?” He said: “Giving water.”"
"6264","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: I heard Shu’bah, narrating on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, narrating on the authority of Sa’d. Ibn Ubadah, that his mother died, so he said: “O Messenger of God, my mother has died, should I give charity on her behalf?” He said: Yes, he said: What kind of charity? Is it better? He said: Irrigating water. That is irrigating Saad in Medina."
"6265","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jafar, On the authority of Salem bin Abi Salem Al-Jishani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abu Dharr, I I see you as weak, and I love for you what I love for myself. Do not appoint two spouses, and do not take charge of the property of an orphan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6266","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hussein, who is Ibn Dhakwan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I am poor and have nothing, and I am an orphan. He said: “Eat from your orphan’s wealth except “He is extravagant, he is not proactive, and he is not imitative.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6267","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Salt told us, he said: Abu Kudaynah told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Saeed, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When this verse was revealed: And do not approach the property of the orphan except in a way that is best, and indeed those who devour the property of He treated orphans unjustly. He said: “The people withheld the orphan’s money and food, and that made it difficult for the people, so they complained about it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: They ask you about the orphans. Say, “Amendment for them is best.” To His statement: “I have cursed you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6268","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Imran bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “Indeed, those who unjustly devour the property of orphans.” He said: “The orphan would be in the lap of the man, and he would be isolated for him.” His food and drink, so that was difficult for the Muslims, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: And if you mix with them, then they are your brothers, and He made it permissible They have their own mixture"
"6269","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Avoid the seven calamities.” It was said: O Messenger of God, what are they? He said: Polytheism to God, And sorcery, and killing a soul which God has forbidden, except for what is right, and consuming usury, and consuming the property of an orphan, and turning away on the day of march, and slander “The chaste, heedless, believing women.”"
"6270","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid, he said: Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, He said: We heard it from Al-Zuhri. Humaid bin Abdul Rahman and Muhammad bin Al-Numan told me, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that his father A boy. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to witness him. He said: “Did your son eat something halal? He said: No. He said: So send him back.” The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
